{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1393181-dead-end-legacies-house-rules-for-half-hearted-lazy-players","id":1393181,"title":"Dead-End Legacies: house rules for half-hearted/lazy players.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-31T13:19:49-07:00","id":1393181,"title":"Dead-End Legacies: house rules for half-hearted/lazy players.","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Convocations and Tetrarchies record thousands of Legacies, most of which have died out having not gained continuity of membership or recorded their Attainments by other means. Hundreds remain dormant as soul stones or daimononika, waiting for the right mage to resurrect them. </div> </div> </div>Many among the Awakened have squandered the potential of their souls by arrogantly passing over tried-and-true legacies that have stood the test of time, attempting to forge their own legacies... and failing. Relatively new mages who define their own legacies too often base them around mysteries or ideals that a more seasoned Willworker would recognize as trivial, spiritually empty, or simply nonsense. Such legacies never attract a following and rarely develop more than one or two attainments.<br /> <br /> But there is a path even more foolhardy and short-sighted than attempting to define one's own legacy prematurely: intentionally joining a legacy that is known to be a dead end. Blinded by the benefits of greater facility with a particular Arcanum or easier access to mana through certain oblations, a reckless mage may shape her soul without regard as to where her chosen legacy leads -- or doesn't.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I often hear that my players want certain immediate benefits from legacy membership, but they can't find a legacy that fits what they want to do with the character, don't want to put in the work to flesh out a full-up legacy that could be part of the game world, and also don't want to wait on the higher Gnosis requirement for making a new personal legacy (or just don't want to put in all the work to define that either). This is particularly true when we know up front that the chronicle isn't going to last for months and months. And I can sympathize with that point of view; if you want a legacy of the same Path as a character with a non-Path ruling Arcanum that isn't Mind then you're probably out of luck because there aren't many of those published. Also coming up with a good legacy is a lot of work and requires a lot of creativity. So, being a person who loves systems, I came up with some house rules for how we can handle that at my table and give my players what they (sometimes) want.<br /> <br /> I know that this isn't going to be appealing for a lot of tables because it explicitly trades what's meant to be an interesting facet of character development for quicker, easier access to in-game advantages. But we tried it out for a relatively short story I wanted to run and it worked out okay for us so I figured I'd share it here. This is the system:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The character obtains the Soul Stone Merit at 2 dots. This is a soul stone of the founder of the failed legacy, who is dead (foolish mages don't live long).</li> <li>The onus is on the player to define the basics of the dead-end legacy: Path, Ruling Arcanum, oblations, yantras, first attainment, and the driving obsession of the mage who founded the legacy. This obsession must be something fairly ridiculous, impossible (per how you run Mage), or trivial. Examples: getting revenge against someone who pissed off the founding mage, planetary-scale non-imperial spellcasting, straightforward effects that can be achieved with Adept-level spells. These kinds of foundations make for bad legacies that lead to no higher truth, but coming up with them is pretty low-effort.</li> <li>The character joins the legacy through usual process from the Soul Stone.</li> <li>In game, it becomes common knowledge that the character joined a known-failed Legacy. This reduces Consilium/Order status by one dot (Sanctity of Merits applies) and caps those Merits at a maximum of 4 dots permanently. This represents the permanent harm a character does to her reputation by joining a dead-end legacy.</li> <li>The character can never develop a second legacy attainment.</li> </ol>This worked out okay for us: The player got to do the thing he wanted to do with his character, we didn't have to spend much time designing a legacy, the whole thing fits into the theme, setting, and rules, and none of this got in the way of the story. Everybody won. Maybe you'll find it handy some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 05-31-2020, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:44:07-07:00","id":1393218,"title":"","content":"I like it, its a shorthand to gain access to yantras and oblations. But its also open ended enough that they can try to refine the philosophy into a fully fleshed Legacy if they so desire. It can be a good plot hook to &quot;prove them wrong&quot;, inherit the torch and refine the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}